 | `vite` | `object` | `{}` | Vite config overrides |
 | `inlineWrappers` | `boolean` | `true` | Compile solid-fuse's built-in wrapper components (`View`, `Text`, `Icon`, `GestureDetector`, `ScrollView`, `Stack`, `Positioned`, `TextField`) as native elements when they are imported by name from `"solid-fuse"`. `<View padding={8}>` then creates its node directly instead of calling a component that spreads its props, which is several times cheaper per element. Behaviour is the same; set `false` to compile them as ordinary components. |
+| `templates` | `boolean \| { group?, pure?, specialize? }` | `false` | **Experimental.** Compile each JSX block of native elements to a module-level template: the static shape (element types, constant props, static text) is sent to Dart once, and every instance is one op carrying only the dynamic values. Components, `<For>`, `<Show>` and refs keep working at the holes; blocks with a spread fall back to the ordinary output. `group` picks how dynamic values share effects (`"roots"`, the default, groups values that read the same source; `"block"`, `"props"`, `"none"`). `pure` treats calls to pure globals and module-level literal tables as static. `specialize` compiles a static copy of a same-module component for call sites whose props are all static. `FUSE_TEMPLATES=1` (or `0`, or `group=block,specialize=0`) overrides the config for one build. The build prints how many blocks were compiled and how many fell back. |
 
